 "id": "ancestor-line",
 "text": "I have joined recently and I need help with my Croatian side. I'm not in Croatia so this is very hard for me. I'm trying to track down my great grandparents and beyond. My great grandfather is Ivan MIHALJEVIĆ and his wife, my great grandmother is Lucija, born FRATROVIĆ. That's kinda all I know about them. They're born likely 1910s and Married late 1930s. They had 5 children and one of them is my grandma born 1942. They lived in Dreznik near Nova Gradiska. I think one of their sons, Franjo, moved away to Slovenia while my grandma went to Slovenia too, then Bosnia and finally settling in Macedonia after she married. The 3 kids stayed in Croatia. If anyone knows them or has them in their tree please let me know because I can't pass them. And their 5 kids are Jana, Mila, Manda, Franjo, and one unknown brother. I have put a picture of Lucija with two of her daughters beside her, Jana and Manda if that helps.",
